    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe requirement: a `POST /api/owners` carrying an `Idempotency-Key` header should, on a repeat with an already-seen key, return the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which the existing duplicate rule would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nI implemented this in keeping with the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (per `AGENTS.md`), rather than adding controller logic.\n\n**Persistence (transaction-consistent, reuses the repository like every other rule)**\n- Added an `idempotencyKey` field/column to the `Owner` entity (`Owner.java`) and the `owners` table in all four schema files (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`). Storing the key on the owner means the key\u2194owner link commits and rolls back atomically with the owner \u2014 no separate in-memory store that could dangle after a rollback.\n\n**New pipeline pieces (each a small single-responsibility unit)**\n- `OwnerIdempotency` \u2014 shared helper that looks up a live (non-soft-deleted) owner by key, mirroring how `RequireUniqueIdentity`/`OwnerIdentities` iterate the repository and ignore deleted owners.\n- `RequestIdempotencyKey` \u2014 a small typed variable so the key flows unambiguously between steps.\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 the new **entry step**: reads the `Idempotency-Key` header, and if that key already produced an owner, responds 200 with it and short-circuits (does not take the `create` flow); otherwise publishes the key and branches into the existing pipeline via `@Flow(\"create\") \u2192 normalizeAddress`. It runs before the body is bound, so the single `@RequestBody` binding rule is preserved.\n- `AssignOwnerIdempotencyKey` \u2014 stamps the key onto the new owner just before `save` (no-op when no key was sent).\n\n**Wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`): added `checkIdempotency` as the first step with `outputs: { create: normalizeAddress }`, and inserted `assignIdempotencyKey` between `flagPossibleDuplicate` and `save`.\n\n## Notable detail\n`@RequestHeader` (Spring MVC) returned `null` through the OfficeFloor bridge, so I used OfficeFloor's native `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")`, which reads the header when present and leaves the value `null` when absent \u2014 exactly the optional-header behavior needed.\n\n## Tests\nFull suite green: `Tests run: 6, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` passes, and the audit log confirms only **one** owner is created across the two identical keyed requests. Existing tests (including keyless creates, which flow through with `null` key) are unaffected.",
