    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here's the ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization:** the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (`owners.POST.yml` `composition.authorize`). Everything below runs inside a single `transaction` governance that spans the pipeline and commits once at the end.\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If a stored owner already has that key, it responds **200** with the existing owner and **short-circuits the whole pipeline** (no create). Otherwise it publishes the key and takes the `create` flow. (Runs before the body is bound.)\n\n2. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 binds the request body (once for the pipeline), canonicalizes the address to normalized form (prefers `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, falls back to flat `address`), and republishes the body.\n\n3. **RequireOwnerFields** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects with **MissingOwnerFieldsException** if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (in its normalized form), `city`, `telephone` is null/blank.\n\n4. **RequirePostcodeInRegion** *(validation)* \u2014 only when a postcode is present: rejects with **InvalidPostcodeException** if it isn't exactly 4 digits, or is out of range for the city's region (per the pinned `PostcodeRange` table; a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit code). Absent postcode is allowed.\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 converts telephone to E.164, mutating the body in place; rejects with **InvalidTelephoneException** if it can't form a valid E.164 number.\n\n6. **RequireTelephoneNationalLength** *(validation)* \u2014 checks the E.164 national-number length against the country calling code (e.g. `+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); rejects with **InvalidTelephoneLengthException** on wrong length.\n\n7. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 only when an email is supplied: validates syntax (rejects with **InvalidEmailException**) and stores it lower-cased in the body. Absent/blank email is left untouched.\n\n8. **RequireOwnerEmailAllowed** *(validation)* \u2014 only when an email is present: rejects with **DisposableEmailException** if the (normalized) domain is on the disposable-mailbox blocklist.\n\n9. **RequireUniqueIdentity** *(validation)* \u2014 the duplicate check, responds **409 DuplicateOwnerException** for either:\n   - *Household duplicate* \u2014 an existing (non-soft-deleted) owner shares the derived `householdId` (same last name + postcode). Skipped if the request opts in with `sharesHousehold`, or if no postcode.\n   - *Identity duplicate* \u2014 an existing owner has the same `identityKey` (telephone + email + household). Always rejects, even for a declared household member.\n   \n   Soft-deleted owners never block. Runs after telephone/email normalization so it compares canonical values.\n\n10. **RequireCityCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects with **409 CityAtCapacityException** if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (exact city-string match).\n\n11. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the DTO into a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n\n12. **AssignOwnerHousehold** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets the owner's `householdId` (derived from last name + postcode). Automatic for every owner regardless of `sharesHousehold`.\n\n13. **AssignOwnerHouseholdSize** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing that `householdId` + 1 (the new owner). No other members \u21d2 size 1.\n\n14. **RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture** *(validation)* \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after the server's current date, rejects with **400 FutureRegistrationDateException**. Validated as supplied, before resolution.\n\n15. **ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent, then rolls a weekend date forward to the next business day. All later date-derived logic uses this adjusted date.\n\n16. **RequireDailyRegistrationCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners are already registered on the resolved (business-day) registration date, rejects with **429 DailyRegistrationLimitException**.\n\n17. **FlagOwnerBulkSignup** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when more than 80 owners are already registered on that day, else false.\n\n18. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; hash of telephone + last name), de-duplicated by appending `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) if it collides with an existing code.\n\n19. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive). Computed before save, so never counts itself.\n\n20. **FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when an existing owner shares last name (case-insensitive) + postcode but has a *different* telephone (lowest matching id chosen). Skipped for a declared household member (`sharesHousehold`) or when postcode is null.\n\n21. **AssignOwnerIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 stamps the request's `Idempotency-Key` onto the owner (only if a key was carried), so future creates with the same key are recognized.\n\n22. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save`.\n\n23. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel/membershipNumber.\n\n24. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with a `Location` header set to the DTO's self-link.\n\n**Note on ordering rationale:** validations are deliberately front-loaded before entity construction (fields \u2192 postcode \u2192 telephone \u2192 email \u2192 uniqueness \u2192 city capacity), and date/capacity checks straddle date resolution (future-date check on the *supplied* value; daily-limit check on the *resolved* business day). The whole thing runs under one transaction that commits only after step 22."
